Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 48/71] Turn on the built-in memories pipeline

With the AGENTS.md refresh gone, durable memory is upstream's memories
pipeline: at session start it extracts memories from earlier rollouts and
consolidates them in a detached session, outside the live conversation's
context. Upstream ships the `memories` feature off by default; the packaged
defaults layer turns it on for this product.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RVZHG9H5htyFpi1B6xbmp8
---
 codex-rs/config/defaults.toml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/codex-rs/config/defaults.toml b/codex-rs/config/defaults.toml
index e91fdc52a4..53c53a070a 100644
--- a/codex-rs/config/defaults.toml
+++ b/codex-rs/config/defaults.toml
@@ -16,3 +16,6 @@ project_root_markers = [".git"]
 
 [history]
 persistence = "save-all"
+
+[features]
+memories = true
